data.content:
Here's what changed and how to fix each piece:

---

**`Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0`** pulls in **`Microsoft.OpenApi` v2**, which has several breaking changes:

### 1. `OpenApiString` removed → use `JsonNode`
```csharp
// Before
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");
// After
param.Schema.Example = JsonNode.Parse("\"1.0\"");
```
Add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes;` and remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;`.

### 2. `OpenApiSecurityScheme.Reference` replaced → use `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference`
```csharp
// Before
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};
// After
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2", null);
```

### 3. Collections may be `null`
`operation.Parameters`, `operation.Responses`, etc. can now be null. Null-check or initialize before use:
```csharp
operation.Responses ??= new OpenApiResponses();
operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });
```

### 4. `OpenApiSchema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's `type: ["string", "null"]` instead of `nullable: true`. Your schema transformer that sets `.Nullable = false` can simply be **removed** — nullability is now handled automatically by the type array.

### 5. Security requirement values need `List<string>`
```csharp
[oAuthScheme] = scopes.ToList()
```

### Fully updated code:
```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters?.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonNode.Parse("\"1.0\"");
    }

    operation.Responses ??= new OpenApiResponses();
    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2", null);
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes.ToList() }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

// The schema transformer setting Nullable = false can be removed entirely.
```
